  "body": "**Maintainer's choice:** move CamCraft's license from MIT to the Apache License 2.0, with copyright held by all CamCraft contributors rather than by the maintainer personally.\n\n**What changes:**\n- `LICENSE`: the full Apache-2.0 text replaces the MIT text.\n- `NOTICE` (new): `Copyright 2026 The CamCraft contributors`, as Apache-2.0 §4(d) expects.\n- `README.md` License section: says Apache-2.0, says the copyright belongs to the contributors, and says contributions are accepted under Apache-2.0 (inbound = outbound, §5).\n- Packaging metadata names the new license:\n  - `aur/LICENSE`, `aur/PKGBUILD`, `aur/.SRCINFO`\n  - the deb/rpm `License:` field in `scripts/package-linux.sh`\n- Packaging scripts that ship `LICENSE` also ship `NOTICE`.\n\n**Why this is possible:** MIT permits sublicensing and redistribution under other terms, so the existing MIT-licensed contributions can be distributed under Apache-2.0. The MIT notice is kept in the decision record. Third-party notices (`assets/ui/LICENSES.md`, clipper2's BSL text) are unaffected.\n\n**Done means:** `LICENSE` is Apache-2.0, `NOTICE` names the contributors, and the README and every packaging manifest say Apache-2.0, with no MIT reference left for CamCraft's own code.\n",
